+## Memo and command-pool reuse
+
+Pipeline and binding-plan memos maintain exact LRU order in reusable indexed slots. Lookups
+allocate no recency nodes; a cached entry handle carries an insertion generation, so eviction
+or replacement invalidates it even when the slot is reused. Both byte and entry limits apply
+before insertion, including byte limits spanning the full `u64` range.
+
+Completed command pools retain the existing global warm-handle budget. Reclamation scans run
+after a pool is returned; allocations do not repeatedly lock and scan an unchanged idle list.
+The return flag is published while holding the pool lock, so concurrent returns are included
+in the current scan or leave a scan pending. Live and in-flight pools are never reclaimed.
+
